Every block landed in components/puck/blocks. Using one takes three lines in components/puck/blocks/index.ts, which your Puck config already spreads.

For example, to use the pricing block:

  import { PricingBlock } from "./pricing/pricing.block";

  P1Pricing: PricingBlock,  // add to p1Blocks

  // in p1Categories — create the entry if it does not exist yet:
  p1Convert: { title: "P1 Convert", components: ["P1Pricing"] },
  // or, if p1Convert already exists, add to its components array (no duplicate key):
  // p1Convert: { title: "P1 Convert", components: ["P1Pricing", "P1CTA"] },

Repeat for each block you want. A block's export name is at the top of components/puck/blocks/<name>/<name>.block.tsx — it does not always match the directory. Review our updates to a block you have edited with `shadcn add @p1/<name> --diff`.
